{
 "text": "# Template: fix an issue with a coding agent. A person approves before any agent\n# call; \"fix\" runs Codex in a bounded loop whose reported_file_scope gate rejects\n# changes outside allowed_paths; a person approves the result before it is recorded.\n# Fill the workspace before running. Agent nodes run through\n#   agentplane run FILE --adapter codex --codex-bin /absolute/path/to/codex --input issue=...\n# Codex authentication needs a named environment reference (for example\n# CODEX_HOME) under config.environment_refs; add it deliberately, it is left out here.\n# The shell node only prints text. Nothing is staged, committed, pushed or sent.\nschema_version: 0\nid: fix-issue\nname: Fix an issue\ninputs:\n  issue: {type: string, required: true}\nnodes:\n  confirm_start:\n    type: human\n    config:\n      prompt: Start the coding agent on this issue? This may use a paid model.\n      context_inputs: [issue]\n    inputs:\n      issue: {type: string, required: true}\n    outputs:\n      decision: {type: string, required: true}\n  fix:\n    type: agent\n    inputs:\n      task: {type: string, required: true}\n      start: {type: string, required: true}\n    config:\n      adapter: codex\n      workspace: /work/repo\n      allowed_paths: [\"src/\", \"tests/\"] # REVIEW: the paths the fix is meant to change\n    outputs:\n      summary: {type: string}\n      changed_files: {type: json}\n    loop:\n      max_attempts: 3\n      gate:\n        inputs:\n          candidate: {type: json, required: true}\n        config:\n          check_id: reported-scope\n          kind: reported_file_scope\n          input: candidate\n          allowed_paths: [\"src/\", \"tests/\"] # REVIEW: keep equal to config.allowed_paths\n      bindings:\n        - {from: candidate.outputs.changed_files, to: gate.inputs.candidate}\n  approve_fix:\n    type: human\n    config:\n      prompt: Review the summary and changed files. Accept the fix? Run your own tests before merging.\n      context_inputs: [summary]\n    inputs:\n      summary: {type: string, required: true}\n      changed_files: {type: json, required: true}\n    outputs:\n      decision: {type: string, required: true}\n  record:\n    type: shell\n    config:\n      command: /usr/bin/printf\n      args: [\"fix accepted\\n\"]\n    inputs:\n      decision: {type: string, required: true}\ngraph_input_bindings:\n  - {from: inputs.issue, to: confirm_start.inputs.issue}\n  - {from: inputs.issue, to: fix.inputs.task}\nedges:\n  - {from: confirm_start.outputs.decision, to: fix.inputs.start}\n  - {from: fix.outputs.summary, to: approve_fix.inputs.summary}\n  - {from: fix.outputs.changed_files, to: approve_fix.inputs.changed_files}\n  - {from: approve_fix.outputs.decision, to: record.inputs.decision}\noutputs: {}\nmetadata:\n  layout:\n    nodes:\n      confirm_start: {x: 0, y: 0}\n      fix: {x: 320, y: 0}\n      approve_fix: {x: 640, y: 0}\n      record: {x: 960, y: 0}\n",
